Yes. Based on the story acceptance criteria and this AddressValidationServiceImpl, I see the main change point clearly.

What the story is asking

Currently, a SendFlex address-validation 4xx error is being treated as an application ERROR and propagated upward. That causes it to appear in the Splunk error/alert dashboard.

The desired behavior is:

1. SendFlex address-validation 4xx/validation failures should be treated as WARN.


2. They should not propagate to the next exception-handling layer as an ERROR.


3. The persisted SendFlex record should have the error/status information set appropriately — the story specifically says NULL errors should not appear in the alert dashboard.


4. Actual unexpected/technical failures should continue to behave as errors.




