Current flow

If SendFlex returns something like:

HTTP 400

the WebClient can throw an exception when this executes:

monoAddressValidationResponse.block();

That exception enters:

catch (Exception exception)

Then you do:

persistAddressValidationFailure(...);

And inside that method:

.statusCode(FAILURE)

Then you do:

throw new ShippingIntegrationException(...)

So the flow becomes:

SendFlex 400
     ↓
WebClient throws exception
     ↓
catch (Exception)
     ↓
persist failure with FAILURE
     ↓
throw ShippingIntegrationException
     ↓
higher layer sees exception
     ↓
ERROR logging
     ↓
Splunk alert

That is exactly what the story is trying to eliminate.


