Recommended structure

I'd change the logic to something along these lines:

try {
    addressValidationResponseDTO = monoAddressValidationResponse.block();

    persistAddressValidationResponse(
        addressValidationRequestDTO,
        addressValidationResponseDTO);

} catch (WebClientResponseException exception) {

    if (exception.getStatusCode().is4xxClientError()) {
        log.warn(
            new LogBuilder()
                .withMessage("SendFlex address validation returned a 4xx validation error")
                .toString());

        persistAddressValidationFailure(
            addressValidationRequestDTO,
            exception);

        return null;
    }

    persistAddressValidationFailure(
        addressValidationRequestDTO,
        exception);

    throw new ShippingIntegrationException(
        "An unexpected error occurred while saving address validation response "
            + exception.getMessage(),
        exception);

} catch (Exception exception) {

    persistAddressValidationFailure(
        addressValidationRequestDTO,
        exception);

    throw new ShippingIntegrationException(
        "An unexpected error occurred while saving address validation response "
            + exception.getMessage(),
        exception);
}

And then specifically for the validation error:

.statusCode(null)

